Concept: “Onchain Week — Behind the Builders”

Goal:
 During Devcon + IBW + ETHGlobal + side events, you become the creator who documents the people building, funding, and shaping Web3.

What you can do throughout the week

1. 🎙️ Founder/Builder Podcast
 Short 5–10 minute conversations:



 What are you building? 

 Why did you start? 

 What problem are you solving? 

 What’s the biggest thing people misunderstand about your project? 

 What are you excited about next? 



Turn one conversation → 5–10 short clips.



2. ⚡ “60 Seconds With a Builder”
 Fast, vertical interviews for Reels/X:

“You have 60 seconds. Explain your startup without using the word blockchain.”

This can become a recognizable recurring format.



3. 👀 “Who’s Building Here?”
 Walk around the event and meet:



 Founders 

 Developers 

 Hackathon winners 

 Investors 

 Creators 

 Protocol teams 

 Interesting community members 



Quick introductions + what they're building.



4. 🧑‍💻 Developer POV
 Make content specifically for developers:

“What are developers actually building at ETHGlobal?”

Show demos, prototypes, hackathon projects and quick technical explanations.



5. 🔥 Daily Recap
 At the end of every day:

DAY 1 — What happened at Devcon/IBW/ETHGlobal?

Include:



 3 people you met 

 3 projects you discovered 

 Best conversation 

 Most interesting demo 

 Your personal takeaway 

 Tomorrow's agenda 



This gives people a reason to come back every day.



6. 🎤 “Ask a Founder”
 Let your audience submit questions before the event.



Example:

“Drop the question you’d ask a Web3 founder if you had 60 seconds 👇”

Then ask those questions on camera and tag the founder.



7. 🏆 “Builder of the Day”
 Every day, highlight one person/project you discovered.



Not a ranking—just a creator spotlight.



8. 🤝 Collaboration Reels
 Instead of only interviewing people, make collaborative content:



 Founder reacts to your take 

 “Explain your startup in 3 words” 

 Founder vs developer rapid-fire 

 “Would you build this in 2026?” 

 Two founders debate a Web3 topic 

 “Pass the mic” — each person introduces another builder 

